<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75469" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχᾰμος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leader, chief,</i> early 
				Ep.
			 only in the phrases 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχαμος ἀνδρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.837
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				96.12
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχαμε λαῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.102
				</span></i>
			, al.; the former applied to the swineherd Eumaeus, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.22
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				121
			</span></i>, and the cowherd Philoetius, <i><span class="en">
				20.185
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				254
			</span></i>.—
				Ep.
			 word, used once by <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄ. στρατοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Pers.</u>
					129
				</span></i>
			(lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρχαμε τ[όξου?]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12.516
				</span></i>
			: in late Poetry without a gen., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.284
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pall.
			</span></i>).</div>
